1) Objective

Build a small, working coding example for an internal Knowledge Management system that:

Hosts unstructured content (e.g., PDF, Word).
Hosts structured content (e.g., tables in an SQL database).
Accepts a natural-language query and determines query intent to route the request to:
unstructured retrieval,
structured retrieval (SQL), or
both (hybrid).
Includes a groundedness / answer validation step so responses are supported by retrieved evidence (documents and/or SQL results).
Candidates may use any LLM/agentic framework
2) Deliverables

Submit the following:

A. Code (required)

Runnable scripts or small repo (preferably GitHub) demonstrating the end-to-end pipeline.
Includes ingestion/indexing for documents and querying for SQL data.
Includes routing by intent and a groundedness/validation step.
B. README (required)

Brief architecture/pipeline description (bullet points are fine).
Key design decisions (frameworks/tools chosen and why).
How intent routing works (structured vs unstructured vs hybrid).
How groundedness/validation works and what happens when evidence is insufficient.
How to run locally (setup, commands, env vars) plus a few example queries.